  "reconstructibility": 2,
  "reason": "The records collectively make the later strategy plausibly reconstructible. R2/R6 and R3 establish SPS consolidation in compositionally similar Al-Co-Fe-Ti-containing HEAs, including dense bulk formation and SPS-induced precipitation, while R1, R13, R14, and R17 show that mechanically alloyed BCC HEA powders can be SPS-consolidated and can develop oxide precipitates. R8 provides particularly strong mechanistic support for protective alumina/chromia and spinel-type oxides in a similar Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni alloy, and R1, R9, and R16 connect processing, oxides or secondary phases with oxidation and corrosion performance. An expert could therefore propose temperature-optimized SPS of the ball-milled BCC powder to obtain densification and protective oxide-bearing microstructures. The exact 1000 °C optimum, the specific AlV2O4/FeAl2O4/FeTiO3 phases, and the detailed chloride-blocking passive-film and biphasic parabolic-oxidation mechanism are not directly disclosed, but they are refinements of a direction already supported by the combined records."
}
